Powerset class ordering, conversion and permutation conventions derived from
pyannote.audio 4.0.7, commit b749285c5cdd4636b2edc7f766f1352c8dde9369.
PyanNet recurrent layout reference: same pyannote.audio commit, using
PyTorch's documented unprojected IFGO LSTM equations. The offline oracle
requires PyTorch; no PyTorch implementation code is included or used at runtime.
SincNet architecture and frame-grid conventions: pyannote.audio commit above.
ParamSincFB even/odd filter construction: asteroid-filterbanks 0.4.0 (MIT),
source SHA256 2df0d1e6f109985c00efcc60970ebceff6a9665c3e65ebae73ea4848e48d8eae.
The MIT permission and warranty notice above applies to these references too.
Segmentation head Linear/leaky-ReLU and LogSoftmax conventions: PyanNet and
pyannote.audio core/model.py at the same commit; source hashes in head fixtures.
StatsPool conversion/weighted unbiased variance: pyannote.audio MIT
models/blocks/pooling.py at the same commit, Copyright (c) 2020- CNRS;
SHA256 8cb687441630e6759fb6ca545d649b41dbec1d42f869954c0a03ae191c7cbd82.
